target macos
om2
note hoppanel: the first cut of Hop's launcher panel as one Omega program, with no Swift. A window with a search
note field and a list of this Mac's apps (the names in /Applications and /System/Applications). Typing narrows the
note list with hopfuzz, the same matcher Hop uses (the functions between the two marker notes come from
note Omega/hopcore.om, put in by Omega/gen-ui.sh), best match first. The first row is selected; the down and up
note arrows move the selection, Enter opens the selected app and ends the program, Escape ends it.
note The field's two delegate methods, the list's two data-source methods and the field's action are Omega code, reached
note through the callback entries (libback; omega-mv seed/ng/a64/DESIGN.md s14).
note With HOPCHECK set in the environment it checks itself instead and opens nothing: it stays in the background,
note types "sa" after half a second, calls its own delegate methods (the text changed; arrow down; Escape) and its
note own action, prints "hoppanel apps N shown H first NAME selected R" and ends after six seconds. Status then: 1
note when apps were found, the typed text narrowed them, the first one was read back from the list's own data
note source, the arrow moved the list's selection and Escape asked to end; 2 to 9 name a failed step.
note Without HOPCHECK the status is 0.
